WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:01.934
-Lil Rel,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:02.901
It's great to see you.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.234
And I want to say
congratulations.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.434
I met backstage
your beautiful fiancée.

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:07.467
-Yeah.
-You are engaged.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:08.567
-I'm engaged.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You are engaged.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.400
I want to hear all about it.
Was it special?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.634
Did you cry?
Where did you do it?

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:14.734
Did you go on one knee?

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:16.334
-Well, let's say this,
first of all,

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.534
since I've been engaged, she's
been on like 15 to 20 brunches.

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.701
People take her out
to eat and dinner.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:23.467
Ain't nobody did nothing for me.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.167
[ Laughter ]
-I'll call you next week.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.367
We'll figure something out.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:28.534
-No, I got one call, he's like,
"You sure?"

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:29.901
And he hung up.
And that was it.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:33.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:36.601
-Where did you do it?
-So look, first of all,

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:39.033
it was a kind of
last-minute decision.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.300
-Okay.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.767
[ Laughter ]
You didn't plan on doing this?

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:46.334
-I didn't plan it at all.
I was so -- we --

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.901
I never told this side
of the story before.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:50.033
So, y'all getting it for real.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.934
So, there's a Chinese buffet
we like to go to.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:54.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.400
-This is a disaster.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.334
This is a complete disaster.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.133
If she comes storming out here,

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.667
I'm letting you --
you're on your own.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:06.167
-On Saturdays, we -- I like --
so, I go to Chinese buffets

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.567
all over the country
for no reason.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.400
I love --
-All you can eat buffet.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.868
-Chicken on a stick,
it's got -- the salt

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.968
and pepper shrimp with the --

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.634
and then they got
a hibachi grill sometimes.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:17.767
-Alright, let's get
to the engagement.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.901
The engagement story.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:22.400
You got engaged.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.000
-I got so happy, like,
"Oh, yeah."

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.701
I mean, the ice cream.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.734
And that weird
chocolate thing that nobody --

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.567
it never cuts off
when it's dripping chocolate.

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:32.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:35.334
No, so, look, we decided to go
to the mall after that

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.534
because we were shopping to go
to a wedding the next day.

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:40.334
-Okay.
-And this is a true story.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.667
I walked past the Tiffany store
because she was in another store

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.234
and I was on the other side
of the mall.

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.701
And I'm like, "Is it time?"

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.667
-Yeah.
-Right.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:51.868
And so, I walked in the store.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.601
I said, "What's up, playboy?"

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.667
The guy was like, "What?"

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:57.367
First of all, he wasn't used
to somebody calling him playboy.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.000
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
"What's up, playboy?"

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.067
-"What's up, playboy?"

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:00.968
-But you see those
beautiful rings.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.167
-I see -- I picked three.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.400
It was three I picked.
I said, "Let me look.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.801
Can I see your
engagement rings?"

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.133
He's like, "Alright."

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.501
And he probably thought
I was like window shopping.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.968
And I was like,
"No, give me that one."

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.434
He's like, "What?"
"Give me that one."

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:12.434
I got to get an outfit,
you know what I mean,

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.567
for this wedding tomorrow.

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:16.200
So I picked the ring out,
I paid for it.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.734
And he was like, "Yo, this is
the fastest --"

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:22.734
-You're like, "Dude,
there's a Chinese buffet

00:02:22.734 --> 00:02:25.501
I got to get to.
I got things to do.

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:26.934
Hurry this up, man."

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:29.667
So, yeah, this is the fastest
sale he's ever got, right?

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:30.801
-That's what it was.

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:34.934
I need to get home after
having a Chinese buffet.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.534
-I got to go to the buffet, man.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:39.901
-I got to get home because...
-Yes, you got things to do.

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:41.334
-It's ice cream,
chicken on the stick.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:43.801
It was a lot of mixtures.
-Chocolate fondue.

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:47.100
-I know, so I had to get home.
-Yes.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.567
-Alright.
Anyway, so I get the ring

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.234
and it's in the Tiffany's bag

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.000
and I'm like, "Oh, man,
I can't let her see that

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.234
I went to the Tiffany store,"
so I'm like,

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:57.534
"Do you got like a plain bag?"
He was excited.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.534
Like, "Ha, do we."
Like, I guess people

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:01.968
do like surprise engagements
and stuff all the time.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:04.133
-You can't walk back out and
go, "What are you doing, honey?"

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.701
"I just went to Tiffany
and got myself something."

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.868
-Yeah, bought me a bracelet and
she's like, "No, you didn't."

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.100
-Yeah, exactly.
-And so I get the ring,

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.067
I get in the car

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:13.701
and I just leave her at the
mall, which is even crazy.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:14.601
She's like, "Yo, where you at?"

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:17.701
"Oh, uh, I'll call you an Uber."

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:20.000
And no.
-Come on,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.501
that's not true at all.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.634
"I'll call you an Uber."
Yeah.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.167
-So look,
I ended up getting in the car

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.267
and I call her dad,
who was in Mississippi.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.167
That's her dad, to get his
blessing and let him know,

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:31.601
which is, you know, you call
an old black man in Mississippi.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.868
That conversation can go --
I was literally -- I said,

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:37.033
"Look, I want to ask your
daughter's hand in marriage.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:38.801
I just wanted your blessing."
He's, "Oh, that's cool.

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.834
But you know, me and Willy
fishing, so, you know."

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:43.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.701
It was such a long conversation
about nothing.

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:49.467
He's like, "What were we talking
about again?" The blessing!

00:03:49.467 --> 00:03:51.701
-I need your blessing.
I need your blessing.

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:52.834
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.667
-And so, you know,
I get his blessing.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:57.234
I call her daughters
and I call my kids

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:58.601
to let them know
what I was doing.

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:00.334
And they was like, "Where
are you going to do it at?"

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:04.167
I said, "Well, I'm taking her
to see Beyoncé on Monday.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.567
I'll do it at
the Beyoncé concert."

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:06.901
-Wow.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:09.167
-And when I decided to do that,
I called Miss Tina,

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:11.367
who I love to death,
which is Beyoncé's mom.

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:12.701
Miss Tina Knowles.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:15.200
-She's so amazing.
-How do you know --

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.167
-How did I meet Miss --
It's a -- So we --

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:18.167
It's a crazy story.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:21.367
So the first time
I ever saw "Black Panther"

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:24.601
was before it came out.
And so this thing about --

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.467
I thought I was going
to a regular screening.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:27.467
I thought it was
like a --

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.634
I thought it was
a special screening,

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.200
but like a regular LA,
like Hollywood screening

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.000
with like a bunch
of people there.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.601
And I show up and it's like,
wait a minute,

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:36.634
this is like --
this is exclusive.

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:38.100
And I didn't really know.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.067
I didn't really know
who was coming for real.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.033
And then, like,
so I invited my friend,

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.501
Hannibal Buress,

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.734
who's staying in the Airbnb
down the street.

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.200
So I was like, "Hey, man, look,
if you want to come through,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.801
come through."
That's before I knew it was like

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:51.133
an exclusive situation.

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:52.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.033
It was very exclusive.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:58.234
So Jerrod Carmichael
was there, DJ Khaled was there.

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:00.367
And then I see, like,
you know, when Beyoncé,

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.100
Jay-Z and Miss Tina
all walk in together,

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.467
they like walk in a triangle.
It's kind of...

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:04.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:07.200
Like with security and then it's
them in the triangle thing.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.501
And they walk in, the wind
blowing and I'm like,

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:10.901
"Oh, this is --"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:13.200
-The wind just blows.
-Just blowing.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.100
-Yeah, yeah yeah.
-It's a theater. How?

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.601
Where the fans at?
Couldn't see the fans.

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:19.667
-That's the Beyoncé effect.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.834
-So they walk in with security
I'm like, wait a minute.

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.300
Is this -- Is this
an exclusive-exclusive thing?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.734
And I tried to hurry up and text
Hannibal like,

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:27.400
"Hey, man, I don't..."
-Yeah, be cool.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.033
-"I don't know if --"
Before I could do that,

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.534
somebody was knocking
on the window.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:31.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:34.400
-You're like, "Hey,
the screening is canceled, dude.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.200
-Like bing boom boom, "Yo, Rel!"

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.501
They yell, "Who invited --
Who invited Hannibal Buress?"

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:44.100
I was like, "I did."
-That's so funny, man.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.100
And so, yeah, I sit next
to Miss Tina during the movie

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.868
and we was talking like
throughout the movie

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:52.634
the whole time.
And man, she was so cool.

00:05:52.634 --> 00:05:54.067
And after we watched the movie

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:55.033
and everybody
walked out the theater,

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:56.467
she left her phone there.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:57.968
And so I grabbed the phone
and I gave it to Jay,

00:05:57.968 --> 00:06:00.334
and I'm like, "Jay,
Miss Tina left her phone."

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:01.667
He's like, "Yeah,
she always do that."

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:06.033
I'm like, "Oh, alright."
And so I give him the phone

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:08.534
and maybe like a couple of days
later after that,

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.367
a good friend of ours,
Robi Reed,

00:06:10.367 --> 00:06:12.267
who's a legendary
casting director,

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:13.968
hit me up and was like,
"Miss Tina

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:15.467
wants you to host her gala."

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:17.901
And I guess, like, she ended up,
like, looking up all my stuff

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.400
after we met
and just thought I was cool.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.901
And from that point on,
she's been

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:24.100
like one of my second moms,
and I appreciate her so much.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.434
-No way.
-Yeah, she's a sweetheart.

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:27.367
-That's a great story.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:30.267
-So you call up...
-I call up Miss Tina

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:31.734
because I'm like --
And it wasn't --

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:33.801
I already bought the ticket,
so I wasn't asking for tickets.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:36.133
Okay, let's get that
out of the way.

00:06:36.133 --> 00:06:37.567
-You're going to see Beyoncé.
-Going to see Beyoncé.

00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:39.734
It was her birthday gift.
She wanted to see Beyoncé.

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:40.968
That's what I got her
for her birthday.

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:42.534
And it was crazy because
it was a last-minute gift.

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:44.734
And I remember I was on the
phone with my other homeboy

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:46.200
and we both trying to
get tickets.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.634
"Rel, your money different.
So we ain't going."

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:52.367
And so we look at --
-The money's different.

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:54.067
-I'm gonna just go take her
to see, I don't know,

00:06:54.067 --> 00:06:55.167
Earth, Wind &amp; Fire or something.

00:06:55.167 --> 00:06:58.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.334 --> 00:07:00.100
-Fire couldn't make it.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.501
I'm just going to see
Earth and Wind.

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:02.567
I'll go see Earth, Wind &amp; Fire.

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.200
-Yeah. I'm gonna see
Earth and Wind.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.601
-Earth and Wind.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.601 --> 00:07:08.534
-I can't even afford Fire.
Yeah. I'm going to see Earth.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:12.467
I'm going to see Earth.
-See the bongo player.

00:07:12.467 --> 00:07:15.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.501
So, you know, I got
the tickets last minute,

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.734
But I called Miss Tina because I
wanted to make sure

00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:21.801
I propose to the right song.

00:07:21.801 --> 00:07:23.934
And it's the Renaissance
concert, so, I'm like,

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:26.934
"Is she even going to do
any of the slow songs?"

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:29.767
Because everything is, "Energy."
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:07:29.767 --> 00:07:32.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.534 --> 00:07:33.801
Wow.

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:36.100
Yeah, no, I got it, yeah, yeah.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:41.334
-And so, I'm like,
alright,

00:07:41.334 --> 00:07:43.701
Miss Tina, what's the perfect
song to propose to?"

00:07:43.701 --> 00:07:46.367
And she was like,
"Well, do it to 'Love on Top.'"

00:07:46.367 --> 00:07:48.734
I'm like, "Oh, okay."
So, what Beyoncé does,

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.567
she stops the song
and lets the audience sing.

00:07:51.567 --> 00:07:53.367
And so that's when
you should do it.

00:07:53.367 --> 00:07:55.033
And I was like, alright,
that'll be perfect.

00:07:55.033 --> 00:07:56.567
That's when I'm going to do it.
And then she was like,

00:07:56.567 --> 00:07:59.501
"Well, I told Jay
that you were proposing.

00:07:59.501 --> 00:08:01.868
And he suggests that we could

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:03.267
put it on the jumbotron
for you."

00:08:03.267 --> 00:08:04.667
And I was like, "Whoa, whoa,
wait a minute, now, I didn't..."

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:06.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.868 --> 00:08:08.467
You know, it's already pressure.

00:08:08.467 --> 00:08:09.801
You know, because you don't
think she's going to say --

00:08:09.801 --> 00:08:11.367
I remember I was talking
to my son about this.

00:08:11.367 --> 00:08:12.901
He's like, "Dad, do you think
she's going to say no?"

00:08:12.901 --> 00:08:15.334
And I never thought about it.
Like, why would you say that?

00:08:15.334 --> 00:08:18.000
-Yeah. Don't put that out there.
Don't put that out there.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.601
-That's what my 13-year-old said
to me,

00:08:19.601 --> 00:08:21.367
"What if she says no?"
And he was like laughing.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.367
I'm like, "What?"

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.501
-"That's an option?
Yeah, I guess you're right."

00:08:26.501 --> 00:08:29.501
-I never thought about that.
It's her choice.

00:08:29.501 --> 00:08:32.200
And so, you know,
she told me "Love on Top."

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.434
And it was even funny
with the story.

00:08:33.434 --> 00:08:35.400
She's like, "Look, Rel, I told,
you know, I told

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:38.234
Beyoncé what's happening.
And you know, she --"

00:08:38.234 --> 00:08:39.601
Look, Beyoncé is a sweetheart,
first of all.

00:08:39.601 --> 00:08:42.267
Let's say that. She's
a sweetheart and it's her show.

00:08:42.267 --> 00:08:45.534
She's like, "Rel want
to do it today? This show?

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.000
On Monday, my birthday show?"

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.601
And it's like --
-Oh, it's her --

00:08:48.601 --> 00:08:49.734
-It was her birthday show.

00:08:49.734 --> 00:08:51.267
And I was like, "Yeah,"
but I didn't --

00:08:51.267 --> 00:08:53.267
First of all, I didn't ask
for all the other stuff

00:08:53.267 --> 00:08:54.834
that came with it.
I was just trying to --

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.767
I was just calling to ask the
song, you know what I mean?

00:08:56.767 --> 00:08:58.501
And everybody else was like,
"Do the jumbotron."

00:08:58.501 --> 00:08:59.767
-You don't even want
to be on the jumbotron.

00:08:59.767 --> 00:09:02.000
-Because she was like,
"Do Rel understand

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.400
I have so much I got to do?"

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.434
I'm like, yeah, I do know
that you got like 15,000 songs.

00:09:07.434 --> 00:09:09.267
You're doing dance
and choreography,

00:09:09.267 --> 00:09:10.601
and I guess we're asking you

00:09:10.601 --> 00:09:11.901
to take some time
for my proposal

00:09:11.901 --> 00:09:13.567
in the middle
of your birthday concert.

00:09:13.567 --> 00:09:15.968
-You're like, "Just give me
the order of the songs,

00:09:15.968 --> 00:09:17.634
so I know when --"
-Well, that's the problem.

00:09:17.634 --> 00:09:18.901
I didn't know the order, right?

00:09:18.901 --> 00:09:21.167
And so --
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:22.934
-So every song you're like --
-I'm literally

00:09:22.934 --> 00:09:24.767
looking at the --
-Getting on one knee.

00:09:24.767 --> 00:09:27.033
-They got the teleprompter.
-And now my next song.

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:28.601
You're like...
-No, no, let me tell you what.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.734
[ Applause ]

00:09:36.734 --> 00:09:41.467
Proposing. Not this song.
Not this song, not yet. No.

00:09:41.467 --> 00:09:43.000
-"How many times you got
to tie your shoes?"

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:50.601
[ Laughter ]

00:09:50.601 --> 00:09:53.267
And so look. But I'm looking
at the teleprompter,

00:09:53.267 --> 00:09:55.534
trying to see if I can
figure out what song is next.

00:09:55.534 --> 00:09:57.033
-That's smart.
-But this is the crazy part.

00:09:57.033 --> 00:09:58.300
It was like,
'cause you know the concert.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:00.701
There's a lot of
beautiful people there,

00:10:00.701 --> 00:10:04.300
a lot of half nakedness. Right?
And so near the prompter

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:07.267
was these these beautiful
half naked women.

00:10:07.267 --> 00:10:10.501
And my fiancée thought --
She was getting mad.

00:10:10.501 --> 00:10:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.267 --> 00:10:15.434
'Cause she didn't know why
I kept looking over there.

00:10:15.434 --> 00:10:17.501
But I was looking
at the teleprompter,

00:10:17.501 --> 00:10:19.834
but I really was looking
at it the whole time.

00:10:19.834 --> 00:10:20.801
It wasn't till
after the proposal.

00:10:20.801 --> 00:10:21.868
She's like, "Oh, you lucky."

00:10:21.868 --> 00:10:22.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.934 --> 00:10:24.434
"You're lucky
that's what that was."

00:10:24.434 --> 00:10:25.767
I thought she was, you know.

00:10:25.767 --> 00:10:28.200
So anyway, you know,

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.701
everybody's having a good time.
They do the "Energy" song.

00:10:30.701 --> 00:10:34.100
Somebody get too energized and
spill they drink on me, right?

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.267
-So you get a drink
spilled on you?

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:36.734
-I get a drink spilled on me.

00:10:36.734 --> 00:10:38.033
And so I'm like,
"I'm gonna go to the bathroom."

00:10:38.033 --> 00:10:41.534
Now, I've been sitting there
for 2 1/2 hours,

00:10:41.534 --> 00:10:42.601
waiting on "Love on Top."

00:10:42.601 --> 00:10:47.167
As -- as soon --
As soon -- as soon --

00:10:47.167 --> 00:10:49.267
And this is the crazy part
about the bathroom story.

00:10:49.267 --> 00:10:51.200
After I washed off
the stuff, I said,

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:52.467
"I'm gonna use the bathroom."

00:10:52.467 --> 00:10:55.334
And as soon as I started
using the bathroom --

00:10:55.334 --> 00:10:56.901
-Okay.
-[ Vocalizing ]

00:10:56.901 --> 00:10:58.767
I was like, "No!" Right?
[ Laughter ]

00:10:58.767 --> 00:11:01.100
And they don't have
real bathrooms.

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:03.734
♪♪

00:11:03.734 --> 00:11:05.067
That's a perfect --
So, because it was a --

00:11:05.067 --> 00:11:06.434
You know, they had
the porta-potties.

00:11:06.434 --> 00:11:09.100
So you imagine hearing somebody
at a lone porta-potty

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.234
yelling like, "No!"

00:11:11.234 --> 00:11:15.534
-Yeah, yeah.
That plastic reverberating.

00:11:15.534 --> 00:11:17.267
-And they had people clean
the porta-potty

00:11:17.267 --> 00:11:21.100
that was all like,
"Is he okay in there?"

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:22.968
-Stay away from that one.
-[ Laughs ]

00:11:22.968 --> 00:11:24.133
I don't know what's happening.

00:11:24.133 --> 00:11:25.367
Someone's getting murdered
in that one.

00:11:25.367 --> 00:11:27.734
Yeah. Oh, my God.
-"No!"

00:11:27.734 --> 00:11:29.200
And, so, I'm trying to hurry up.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.267
You know, I'm in my 40s,
so I couldn't do a stoppage.

00:11:31.267 --> 00:11:32.968
You know what I mean?
I'm too old to do that.

00:11:32.968 --> 00:11:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:35.601
I had to --
You know what I mean?

00:11:35.601 --> 00:11:37.167
I had to -- I had get out
of there. You know what I mean?

00:11:37.167 --> 00:11:38.400
It's 2 1/2 hours.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.801
-Yeah, you gotta --
You gotta follow through.

00:11:39.801 --> 00:11:41.267
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.267 --> 00:11:44.501
-And, so, I start running back
to the seat.

00:11:44.501 --> 00:11:46.534
And I get to the seats

00:11:46.534 --> 00:11:49.133
and I literally forget --
It looked like they moved --

00:11:49.133 --> 00:11:51.267
'cause Beyoncé kept making
all these demands.

00:11:51.267 --> 00:11:52.934
So I'm like, "Did she tell
the crowd to change seats?

00:11:52.934 --> 00:11:55.100
Like, where are my seats?"

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:56.300
-You couldn't find your seat.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:11:58.868
-I couldn't find the seat.
I had to run back.

00:11:58.868 --> 00:12:01.267
And by this time, they doin' --
Now they doin' the --

00:12:01.267 --> 00:12:02.934
The crowd is singing, right?

00:12:02.934 --> 00:12:06.334
-This is your part.
-This is my part.

00:12:06.334 --> 00:12:09.601
And, so, I'm run out, run back,
retrace my steps like,

00:12:09.601 --> 00:12:11.734
"Okay, it was over here,
and then I started --

00:12:11.734 --> 00:12:13.067
That brother's eating popcorn,
and then --"

00:12:13.067 --> 00:12:14.467
Like, you know what I mean?

00:12:14.467 --> 00:12:15.634
And, so, I end up
finding the seat,

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:17.434
'cause I can see
the cameraman sweating, like,

00:12:17.434 --> 00:12:19.133
on his earpiece like, "I don't
know where he at, man,"

00:12:19.133 --> 00:12:20.634
you know?

00:12:20.634 --> 00:12:21.968
And then the crowd sound like
they started getting irritated,

00:12:21.968 --> 00:12:25.033
'cause they been singing
the a cappella for so long.

00:12:25.033 --> 00:12:27.434
People was like,
"Baby, it's you?

00:12:27.434 --> 00:12:29.701
You're the --
Why are we still singin' this?"

00:12:29.701 --> 00:12:30.868
And then, at some point,
I swear to you,

00:12:30.868 --> 00:12:33.934
Beyoncé was like...

00:12:33.934 --> 00:12:36.634
And that's when I got
on one knee and I proposed.

00:12:36.634 --> 00:12:38.200
And this is the thing about it.
I don't care.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:41.167
Go watch any proposal videos,
especially with black women.

00:12:41.167 --> 00:12:42.434
Every time they get proposed to,

00:12:42.434 --> 00:12:44.534
they do this weird thing
where they walk --

00:12:44.534 --> 00:12:46.067
they step in and walk back.

00:12:46.067 --> 00:12:47.434
It's like they don't believe it.

00:12:47.434 --> 00:12:50.033
It's like -- So --
I get -- I got up on one knee,

00:12:50.033 --> 00:12:51.601
and this is
really what happened.

00:12:51.601 --> 00:12:52.868
I did the one-knee thing,
and the first thing she did say,

00:12:52.868 --> 00:12:53.968
"What you doing down there?"

00:12:53.968 --> 00:12:56.501
You know?
"Why don't you get up?"

00:12:56.501 --> 00:12:57.634
I was like, "Baby, I'm tryin'
to propose to you."

00:12:57.634 --> 00:12:58.968
"You tryin' to do what?"

00:12:58.968 --> 00:13:07.901
She's like, "Noooooooooo!

00:13:07.901 --> 00:13:12.367
Aah! Aah!"

00:13:12.367 --> 00:13:14.367
-[ Laughs ]

00:13:19.234 --> 00:13:20.834
You got to do --
You know, they do this.

00:13:20.834 --> 00:13:22.534
[ Laughter ]

00:13:22.534 --> 00:13:23.834
She was, like,
cussing me out about,

00:13:23.834 --> 00:13:25.868
"You gon' make my makeup --"
and all this other stuff.

00:13:25.868 --> 00:13:28.534
And she said "yes."
-There you go!

00:13:28.534 --> 00:13:29.901
That's what I'm talking about.

00:13:29.901 --> 00:13:31.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I'm talking about.

00:13:31.534 --> 00:13:33.534
Well done.

00:13:33.534 --> 00:13:34.934
That is how you do it.

00:13:34.934 --> 00:13:36.100
-Yes.
-She's gorgeous.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:38.634
And congratulations
to you, buddy.

00:13:38.634 --> 00:13:41.634
Gosh, that's a great story.

00:13:41.634 --> 00:13:44.400
Can you tell me about this --
you and Tiffany Haddish on tour?

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:46.367
-Yes. This is my best friend.
I don't know if you know.

00:13:46.367 --> 00:13:49.167
The very funny,
hilarious Tiffany Haddish.

00:13:49.167 --> 00:13:50.934
-She's unbelievable.
She is hilarious.

00:13:50.934 --> 00:13:52.534
-And, you know,
since we've been on strike,

00:13:52.534 --> 00:13:55.100
a lot of us had to go back on
the road to make some money.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.667
And so -- But, anyway,
I love stand-up.

00:13:56.667 --> 00:13:57.968
That's our roots.
That's how we met.

00:13:57.968 --> 00:13:59.968
That's how we became friends.

00:13:59.968 --> 00:14:03.133
She was my first L.A. friend,
like, who would pick me up

00:14:03.133 --> 00:14:06.501
from the airport, in the loudest
Geo Metro you can think of.

00:14:06.501 --> 00:14:07.934
But I couldn't wait to hear
that Geo Metro coming.

00:14:07.934 --> 00:14:09.434
"That's my ride!"

00:14:09.434 --> 00:14:10.601
-That's what I was getting at.

00:14:10.601 --> 00:14:12.400
-And -- But this is
our tour, man. We both --

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:15.133
-But I remember, didn't you do,
like, auditions together

00:14:15.133 --> 00:14:16.734
and help each other out and --

00:14:16.734 --> 00:14:18.734
-Auditions. I used to, like --
She used to let me crash

00:14:18.734 --> 00:14:20.033
on her couch, right?

00:14:20.033 --> 00:14:21.801
She used to have her printer
to print out her signs

00:14:21.801 --> 00:14:24.501
