those little TV tables,

00:14:24.501 --> 00:14:26.267
so it was always shaking.

00:14:26.267 --> 00:14:27.801
-Once the printer
starts going...

00:14:27.801 --> 00:14:29.667
-Yeah. This was a TV table.

00:14:29.667 --> 00:14:32.167
Like, "Why can't I eat my food?
I guess in my lap."

00:14:32.167 --> 00:14:34.601
But, no, it's, like,
grinding with somebody like that

00:14:34.601 --> 00:14:39.200
for so long, watching her obtain
all the success she has,

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:41.534
and vice versa, and we've been
friends for a very long --

00:14:41.534 --> 00:14:42.701
That's how we met.

00:14:42.701 --> 00:14:45.100
We met when we was doing
a stand-up series called

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:47.601
"Bill Bellamy's
Who's Got Jokes?" on TV One.

00:14:47.601 --> 00:14:50.734
And I won my episode in Chicago.
She won hers in L.A.

00:14:50.734 --> 00:14:52.300
And I'm backstage --
You know, I'm like, hype

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.567
